From 7797acf3b22e4849923e4ae61ad0491042b3bbf9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ga=C3=ABl=20Duval?= <gael@murena.io>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 12:52:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(templates): Word defaults for blank documents

Every new/<locale>/new.docx now starts like a blank Word document:
- body text in the theme body font (Calibri), 11 pt, 8 pt after,
  line spacing 1.08;
- Office theme: Calibri Light / Calibri and the colour scheme of
  Word 2013-2021 (accent 1 = 4472C4);
- Word's built-in styles written out explicitly (Heading 1-9 in Calibri
  Light with the Word 2016 colours, Title, Subtitle, Quote, Intense
  Quote, emphasis and reference character styles, List Paragraph,
  No Spacing, Table Grid), so the document looks the same in any Word.
Language, page size, margins, settings, latent styles and the
right-to-left paragraph default of each locale are kept. Calibri renders
with the metric-compatible Carlito (OFL, shipped in core-fonts) when it
is not installed.

Generated by tools/word-defaults/make_blank_docx.py (ElixirOffice repo).

[branding]

Assisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
